{"object":"Charging suitability depends on voltage, current, completion behavior, heat, and device or charger control. Those generic factors require inspecting the actual phone, charger, cable, and protocol rather than assuming that higher advertised wattage is always compatible, faster, safer, or more durable.","predicate":"requires","source_url":"http://localhost:8090/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic/Battery_charger","subject":"charging protocol boundary","text":"A charging protocol governs voltage, current and completion behavior, while chargers may monitor temperature and voltage and charging current generates heat. Compatibility and risk therefore depend on the actual device, charger, cable and protocol rather than advertised wattage alone.","title":"prop_charging_protocol_scope"}